From: rolotrealanis98 <122947376+rolotrealanis98@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:58:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] dt-bindings: cpufreq: apple,cluster-cpufreq: Add T6050

The T6050 (M5 Pro) cluster DVFS block has the T8112 register layout:
p-state request in bits 4:0 of the command register at +0x20, current
p-state in bits 9:5 of the status register at +0x50 (measured on the
J714s and J716s). Like T6020 it is described as
"apple,t6050-cluster-cpufreq", "apple,t8112-cluster-cpufreq".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml    | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml
index b51913a81..c96ce28f2 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml
@@ -36,7 +36,9 @@ properties:
           - const: apple,s5l8960x-cluster-cpufreq
       - const: apple,s5l8960x-cluster-cpufreq
       - items:
-          - const: apple,t6020-cluster-cpufreq
+          - enum:
+              - apple,t6020-cluster-cpufreq
+              - apple,t6050-cluster-cpufreq
           - const: apple,t8112-cluster-cpufreq
 
   reg:
